External services consulted
---------------------------

drand (https://drand.love)
    Operated by the League of Entropy (Cloudflare, Protocol Labs, EPFL,
    and other participants). VAJRA consumes the public drand beacon for
    wall-clock anchoring; no VAJRA code is included in or executed by drand
    itself.

IPFS / Kubo (https://github.com/ipfs/kubo)
    MIT / Apache License 2.0 (dual)
    Used as the distribution layer. VAJRA interacts with Kubo over its
    HTTP RPC; no VAJRA code is included in or executed by IPFS itself.


=============================================================================

The cryptographic constructions used in VAJRA are based on published academic
work and standard primitives. Specifically:

  - Time-lock puzzle construction by Rivest, Shamir, and Wagner (MIT, 1996):
    "Time-lock puzzles and timed-release Crypto."

  - Secret sharing construction by Adi Shamir (1979):
    "How to share a secret." Communications of the ACM, 22(11), 612–613.

  - X25519 Diffie–Hellman exchange by Daniel J. Bernstein (2006).

  - ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD by Daniel J. Bernstein (2008), as specified in
    RFC 8439.

  - drand distributed randomness beacon (Cloudflare et al., 2018-present).

VAJRA does not claim original cryptographic invention. It composes
well-understood primitives into an examination-distribution-specific
protocol. This NOTICE acknowledges that lineage.
